<span class=text-black-100/70>No credit card required.</span></div></div><div class="absolute -bottom-2.5 -right-2.5 h-full w-full rounded-xl border-2 border-black-100/20 bg-black-100"></div></div></div></div></section><section id=faqs class="py-12 sm:pb-20 sm:pt-14"><div class="container flex flex-col gap-10 px-4 mx-auto max-w-7xl md:gap-16"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-center text-black-100 md:text-4xl">Web Scraping API FAQs</h2><div class="flex flex-col gap-4 mx-auto w-full max-w-4xl"><div data-faq-index=0 data-faq-expanded=true class="faq-item flex gap-4 items-start px-6 py-5 rounded-md border duration-200 cursor-pointer bg-yellow-100 border-[#BD9002]"><div class="flex flex-col flex-1 gap-4"><div class="text-base font-bold text-black-100 md:text-lg">What is a web scraping API?</div><div class="faq-answer flex flex-col gap-3 text-sm text-black-100 md:text-base"><p>A web scraping API is a tool that collects data from websites through an API request. You send a URL and get the page HTML, rendered content, or structured data back. It lets you scrape websites without managing proxies, browsers, retries, or blocking issues yourself.</p></div></div><div class=flex-shrink-0><svg class="faq-icon-close flex-shrink-0" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M17.0711 2.92898c-3.9053-3.90522-10.23695-3.90522-14.14217.0-3.905437 3.90544-3.905216 10.23692.0 14.14212 3.90544 3.9055 10.23667 3.9055 14.14217.0 3.9052-3.9052 3.9054-10.23668.0-14.14212zM3.79889 16.2012C.387325 12.7896.401247 7.22443 3.81284 3.81283c3.41157-3.411566 8.96276-3.411566 12.37436.0 3.4116 3.41157 3.4116 8.96277.0 12.37437C12.7757 19.5988 7.21046 19.6127 3.79889 16.2012zm9.73661-3.5495L10.8839 10l2.6516-2.6516c.244-.24396.244-.63994.0-.88389C13.2916 6.22056 12.8956 6.22056 12.6517 6.46451L10 9.11616 7.34835 6.46451c-.24395-.24395-.63993-.24395-.88388.0-.24396.24395-.24396.639930000000001.0.88389L9.11612 10 6.46447 12.6517C6.22051 12.8956 6.22051 13.2916 6.46447 13.5356c.24395.2439.63993.2439.88388.0L10 10.8839l2.6517 2.6517C12.8956 13.7795 13.2916 13.7795 13.5355 13.5356 13.7795 13.2916 13.7795 12.8956 13.5355 12.6517z" fill="#000"/></svg>
<svg class="faq-icon-plus flex-shrink-0" style="display:none" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M10 0C4.47719.0.0 4.47719.0 10c0 5.5231 4.47719 10 10 10 5.5231.0 10-4.4769 10-10C20 4.47719 15.5231.0 10 0zm0 18.7697c-4.82469.0-8.75-3.945-8.75-8.76974.0-4.82469 3.92531-8.75 8.75-8.75 4.8247.0 8.75 3.92533 8.75 8.75.0 4.82464-3.9253 8.76974-8.75 8.76974zM14.375 9.375h-3.75V5.625C10.625 5.28 10.345 5 10 5s-.625.28-.625.625v3.75H5.625C5.28 9.375 5 9.655 5 10s.28.625.625.625h3.75v3.75C9.375 14.72 9.655 15 10 15S10.625 14.72 10.625 14.375v-3.75h3.75C14.72 10.625 15 10.345 15 10S14.72 9.375 14.375 9.375z" fill="#000"/></svg></div></div><div data-faq-index=1 data-faq-expanded=false class="faq-item flex gap-4 items-start px-6 py-5 rounded-md border duration-200 cursor-pointer bg-gray-50 border-black-100/10"><div class="flex flex-col flex-1 gap-4"><div class="text-base font-bold text-black-100 md:text-lg">How do I set up and use a web scraping API?</div><div class="faq-answer flex flex-col gap-3 text-sm text-black-100 md:text-base" style=display:none><p>To use a web scraping API, create an account, get your API key, and send a request to the endpoint you need. Add the target URL and choose options such as JavaScript rendering, proxy type, geotargeting, screenshots, Markdown output, or JSON extraction.</p><p>With ScrapingBee, you can also build the request visually in the dashboard. Choose your endpoint, set your parameters, send a test request, and view the response. To extract data as JSON, use CSS or XPath rules, or describe what you need with AI extraction.</p></div></div><div class=flex-shrink-0><svg class="faq-icon-close flex-shrink-0" style="display:none" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M17.0711 2.92898c-3.9053-3.90522-10.23695-3.90522-14.14217.0-3.905437 3.90544-3.905216 10.23692.0 14.14212 3.90544 3.9055 10.23667 3.9055 14.14217.0 3.9052-3.9052 3.9054-10.23668.0-14.14212zM3.79889 16.2012C.387325 12.7896.401247 7.22443 3.81284 3.81283c3.41157-3.411566 8.96276-3.411566 12.37436.0 3.4116 3.41157 3.4116 8.96277.0 12.37437C12.7757 19.5988 7.21046 19.6127 3.79889 16.2012zm9.73661-3.5495L10.8839 10l2.6516-2.6516c.244-.24396.244-.63994.0-.88389C13.2916 6.22056 12.8956 6.22056 12.6517 6.46451L10 9.11616 7.34835 6.46451c-.24395-.24395-.63993-.24395-.88388.0-.24396.24395-.24396.639930000000001.0.88389L9.11612 10 6.46447 12.6517C6.22051 12.8956 6.22051 13.2916 6.46447 13.5356c.24395.2439.63993.2439.88388.0L10 10.8839l2.6517 2.6517C12.8956 13.7795 13.2916 13.7795 13.5355 13.5356 13.7795 13.2916 13.7795 12.8956 13.5355 12.6517z" fill="#000"/></svg>
<svg class="faq-icon-plus flex-shrink-0" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M10 0C4.47719.0.0 4.47719.0 10c0 5.5231 4.47719 10 10 10 5.5231.0 10-4.4769 10-10C20 4.47719 15.5231.0 10 0zm0 18.7697c-4.82469.0-8.75-3.945-8.75-8.76974.0-4.82469 3.92531-8.75 8.75-8.75 4.8247.0 8.75 3.92533 8.75 8.75.0 4.82464-3.9253 8.76974-8.75 8.76974zM14.375 9.375h-3.75V5.625C10.625 5.28 10.345 5 10 5s-.625.28-.625.625v3.75H5.625C5.28 9.375 5 9.655 5 10s.28.625.625.625h3.75v3.75C9.375 14.72 9.655 15 10 15S10.625 14.72 10.625 14.375v-3.75h3.75C14.72 10.625 15 10.345 15 10S14.72 9.375 14.375 9.375z" fill="#000"/></svg></div></div><div data-faq-index=2 data-faq-expanded=false class="faq-item flex gap-4 items-start px-6 py-5 rounded-md border duration-200 cursor-pointer bg-gray-50 border-black-100/10"><div class="flex flex-col flex-1 gap-4"><div class="text-base font-bold text-black-100 md:text-lg">What type of data can I extract with a web scraper API?</div><div class="faq-answer flex flex-col gap-3 text-sm text-black-100 md:text-base" style=display:none><p>With a web scraper API, you can extract data from public web pages, including product listings, prices, reviews, search results, real estate listings, job posts, news articles, company pages, and more. With AI extraction, you can also ask for specific fields in natural language instead of writing custom parsing logic for each website.</p></div></div><div class=flex-shrink-0><svg class="faq-icon-close flex-shrink-0" style="display:none" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M17.0711 2.92898c-3.9053-3.90522-10.23695-3.90522-14.14217.0-3.905437 3.90544-3.905216 10.23692.0 14.14212 3.90544 3.9055 10.23667 3.9055 14.14217.0 3.9052-3.9052 3.9054-10.23668.0-14.14212zM3.79889 16.2012C.387325 12.7896.401247 7.22443 3.81284 3.81283c3.41157-3.411566 8.96276-3.411566 12.37436.0 3.4116 3.41157 3.4116 8.96277.0 12.37437C12.7757 19.5988 7.21046 19.6127 3.79889 16.2012zm9.73661-3.5495L10.8839 10l2