<svg class="faq-icon-plus flex-shrink-0" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M10 0C4.47719.0.0 4.47719.0 10c0 5.5231 4.47719 10 10 10 5.5231.0 10-4.4769 10-10C20 4.47719 15.5231.0 10 0zm0 18.7697c-4.82469.0-8.75-3.945-8.75-8.76974.0-4.82469 3.92531-8.75 8.75-8.75 4.8247.0 8.75 3.92533 8.75 8.75.0 4.82464-3.9253 8.76974-8.75 8.76974zM14.375 9.375h-3.75V5.625C10.625 5.28 10.345 5 10 5s-.625.28-.625.625v3.75H5.625C5.28 9.375 5 9.655 5 10s.28.625.625.625h3.75v3.75C9.375 14.72 9.655 15 10 15S10.625 14.72 10.625 14.375v-3.75h3.75C14.72 10.625 15 10.345 15 10S14.72 9.375 14.375 9.375z" fill="#000"/></svg></div></div><div data-faq-index=4 data-faq-expanded=false class="faq-item flex gap-4 items-start px-6 py-5 rounded-md border duration-200 cursor-pointer bg-gray-50 border-black-100/10"><div class="flex flex-col flex-1 gap-4"><div class="text-base font-bold text-black-100 md:text-lg">How long does it take to get the scraping results?</div><div class="faq-answer flex flex-col gap-3 text-sm text-black-100 md:text-base" style=display:none><p>It depends on the target website and the features you enable. Fast Search API requests usually return scraping results in under a second. E-commerce API requests have a median response time of around 2.5 seconds. Standard scraping API requests can take longer when JavaScript rendering, premium proxies, or advanced anti-bot handling are enabled.</p></div></div><div class=flex-shrink-0><svg class="faq-icon-close flex-shrink-0" style="display:none" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M17.0711 2.92898c-3.9053-3.90522-10.23695-3.90522-14.14217.0-3.905437 3.90544-3.905216 10.23692.0 14.14212 3.90544 3.9055 10.23667 3.9055 14.14217.0 3.9052-3.9052 3.9054-10.23668.0-14.14212zM3.79889 16.2012C.387325 12.7896.401247 7.22443 3.81284 3.81283c3.41157-3.411566 8.96276-3.411566 12.37436.0 3.4116 3.41157 3.4116 8.96277.0 12.37437C12.7757 19.5988 7.21046 19.6127 3.79889 16.2012zm9.73661-3.5495L10.8839 10l2.6516-2.6516c.244-.24396.244-.63994.0-.88389C13.2916 6.22056 12.8956 6.22056 12.6517 6.46451L10 9.11616 7.34835 6.46451c-.24395-.24395-.63993-.24395-.88388.0-.24396.24395-.24396.639930000000001.0.88389L9.11612 10 6.46447 12.6517C6.22051 12.8956 6.22051 13.2916 6.46447 13.5356c.24395.2439.63993.2439.88388.0L10 10.8839l2.6517 2.6517C12.8956 13.7795 13.2916 13.7795 13.5355 13.5356 13.7795 13.2916 13.7795 12.8956 13.5355 12.6517z" fill="#000"/></svg>
<svg class="faq-icon-plus flex-shrink-0" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M10 0C4.47719.0.0 4.47719.0 10c0 5.5231 4.47719 10 10 10 5.5231.0 10-4.4769 10-10C20 4.47719 15.5231.0 10 0zm0 18.7697c-4.82469.0-8.75-3.945-8.75-8.76974.0-4.82469 3.92531-8.75 8.75-8.75 4.8247.0 8.75 3.92533 8.75 8.75.0 4.82464-3.9253 8.76974-8.75 8.76974zM14.375 9.375h-3.75V5.625C10.625 5.28 10.345 5 10 5s-.625.28-.625.625v3.75H5.625C5.28 9.375 5 9.655 5 10s.28.625.625.625h3.75v3.75C9.375 14.72 9.655 15 10 15S10.625 14.72 10.625 14.375v-3.75h3.75C14.72 10.625 15 10.345 15 10S14.72 9.375 14.375 9.375z" fill="#000"/></svg></div></div><div data-faq-index=5 data-faq-expanded=false class="faq-item flex gap-4 items-start px-6 py-5 rounded-md border duration-200 cursor-pointer bg-gray-50 border-black-100/10"><div class="flex flex-col flex-1 gap-4"><div class="text-base font-bold text-black-100 md:text-lg">Who is ScrapingBee built for?</div><div class="faq-answer flex flex-col gap-3 text-sm text-black-100 md:text-base" style=display:none><p>ScrapingBee is built for developers, founders, and product teams that need web data in their apps, workflows, or internal tools. It's ideal for teams that want to collect data at scale without managing proxies, browsers, anti-bot systems, or scraper maintenance. Common use cases include e-commerce, AI, cybersecurity, market intelligence, fintech, and go-to-market tools.</p></div></div><div class=flex-shrink-0><svg class="faq-icon-close flex-shrink-0" style="display:none" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M17.0711 2.92898c-3.9053-3.90522-10.23695-3.90522-14.14217.0-3.905437 3.90544-3.905216 10.23692.0 14.14212 3.90544 3.9055 10.23667 3.9055 14.14217.0 3.9052-3.9052 3.9054-10.23668.0-14.14212zM3.79889 16.2012C.387325 12.7896.401247 7.22443 3.81284 3.81283c3.41157-3.411566 8.96276-3.411566 12.37436.0 3.4116 3.41157 3.4116 8.96277.0 12.37437C12.7757 19.5988 7.21046 19.6127 3.79889 16.2012zm9.73661-3.5495L10.8839 10l2.6516-2.6516c.244-.24396.244-.63994.0-.88389C13.2916 6.22056 12.8956 6.22056 12.6517 6.46451L10 9.11616 7.34835 6.46451c-.24395-.24395-.63993-.24395-.88388.0-.24396.24395-.24396.639930000000001.0.88389L9.11612 10 6.46447 12.6517C6.22051 12.8956 6.22051 13.2916 6.46447 13.5356c.24395.2439.63993.2439.88388.0L10 10.8839l2.6517 2.6517C12.8956 13.7795 13.2916 13.7795 13.5355 13.5356 13.7795 13.2916 13.7795 12.8956 13.5355 12.6517z" fill="#000"/></svg>
<svg class="faq-icon-plus flex-shrink-0" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M10 0C4.47719.0.0 4.47719.0 10c0 5.5231 4.47719 10 10 10 5.5231.0 10-4.4769 10-10C20 4.47719 15.5231.0 10 0zm0 18.7697c-4.82469.0-8.75-3.945-8.75-8.76974.0-4.82469 3.92531-8.75 8.75-8.75 4.8247.0 8.75 3.92533 8.75 8.75.0 4.82464-3.9253 8.76974-8.75 8.76974zM14.375 9.375h-3.75V5.625C10.625 5.28 10.345 5 10 5s-.625.28-.625.625v3.75H5.625C5.28 9.375 5 9.655 5 10s.28.625.625.625h3.75v3.75C9.375 14.72 9.655 15 10 15S10.625 14.72 10.625 14.375v-3.75h3.75C14.72 10.625 15 10.345 15 10S14.72 9.375 14.375 9.375z" fill="#000"/></svg></div></div><div data-faq-index=6 data-faq-expanded=false class="faq-item flex gap-4 items-start px-6 py-5 rounded-md border duration-200 cursor-pointer bg-gray-50 border-black-100/10"><div class="flex flex-col flex-1 gap-4"><div class="text-base font-bold text-black-100 md:text-lg">How fast is ScrapingBee's API, and can it handle difficult websites?</div><div class="faq-answer flex flex-col gap-3 text-sm text-black-100 md:text-base" style=display:none><p>Scraper response times depend on the target website and enabled features. Simple scraping requests are faster, while JavaScript rendering and advanced anti-bot handling take longer. For complex sites, ScrapingBee uses browser rendering with rotating, premium, and stealth proxies so you don't have to build that infrastructure yourself.</p></div></div><div class=flex-shrink-0><svg class="faq-icon-close flex-shrink-0" style="display:none" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M17.0711 2.92898c-3.9053-3.90522-10.23695-3.90522-14.14217.0-3.905437 3.90544-3.905216 10.23692.0 14.14212 3.90544 3.9055 10.23667 3.9055 14.14217.0 3.9052-3.9052 3.9054-10.23668.0-14.14212zM3.79889 16.2012C.387325 12.7896.401247 7.22443 3.81284 3.81283c3.41157-3.411566 8.96276-3.411566 12.37436.0 3.4116 3.41157 3.4116 8.96277.0 12.37437C12.7757 19.5988 7.21046 19.6127 3.79889 16.2012zm9.73661-3.5495L10.8839 10l2.6516-2.6516c.244-.24396.244-.63994.0-.88389C13.2916 6.22056 12.8956 6.22056 12.6517 6.46451L10 9.11616 7.34835 6.46451c-.24395-.24395-.63993-.24395-.88388.0-.24396.24395-.24396.639930000000001.0.88389L9.11612 10 6.46447 12.6517C6.22051 12.8956 6.22051 13.2916 6.46447 13.5356c.24395.2439.63993.2439.88388.0L10 10.8839l2.6517 2.6517C12.8956 13.7795 13.2916 13.7795 13.5355 13.5356 13.7795 13.2916 13.7795 12.8956 13.5355 12.6517z" fill="#000"/></svg>
<svg class="faq-icon-plus flex-shrink-0" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M10 0C4.47719.0.0 4.47719.0 10c0 5.5231 4.47719 10 10 10 5.5231.0 10-4.4769 10-10C20 4.47719 15.5231.0 10 0zm0 18.7697c-4.82469.0-8.75-3.945-8.75-8.76974.0-4.82469 3.92531-8.75 8.75-8.75 4.8247.0 8.75 3.92533 8.75 8.75.0 4.82464-3.9253 8.76974-8.75 8.76974zM14.375 9.375h-3.75V5.625C10.625 5.28 10.345 5 10 5s-.625.28-.625.625v3.75H5.625C5.28 9.375 5 9.655 5 10s.28.625.625.625h3.75v3.75C9.375 14.72 9.655 15 10 15S10.625 14.72 10.625 14.375v-3.75h3.75C14.72 10.625 15 10.345 15 10S14.72 9.375 14.375 9.375z" fill="#000"/></svg></div></div><div data-faq-index=7 data-faq-expanded=false class="faq-item flex gap-4 items-start px-6 py-5 rounded-md border duration-200 cursor-pointer bg-gray-50 border-black-100/10"><div class="flex flex-col flex-1 gap-4"><div class="text-base font-bold text-black-100 md:text-lg">Is ScrapingBee's web scraper API SOC 2 compliant?</div><div class="faq-answer flex flex-col gap-3 text-sm text-black-100 md:text-base" style=display:none><p>Yes. ScrapingBee's web scraper API is SOC 2 Type II compliant, with controls audited and verified by an independent auditor.</p></div></div><div class=flex-shrink-0><svg class="faq-icon-close flex-shrink-0" style="display:none" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M17.0711 2.92898c-3.9053-3.90522-10.23695-3.90522-14.14217.0-3.905437 3.90544-3.905216 10.23692.0 14.14212 3.90544 3.9055 10.23667 3.9055 14.14217.0 3.9052-3.9052 3.9054-10.23668.0-14.14212zM3.79889 16.2012C.387325 12.7896.401247 7.22443 3.81284 3.81283c3.41157-3.411566 8.96276-3.411566 12.37436.0 3.4116 3.41157 3.4116 8.96277.0 12.37437C12.7757 19.5988 7.21046 19.6127 3.79889 16.2012zm9.73661-3.5495L10.8839 10l2.6516-2.6516c.244-.24396.244-.63994.0-.88389C13.2916 6.22056 12.8956 6.22056 12.6517 6.46451L10 9.11616 7.34835 6.46451c-.24395-.24395-.63993-.24395-.88388.0-.24396.24395-.24396.639930000000001.0.88389L9.11612 10 6.46447 12.6517C6.22051 12.8956 6.22051 13.2916 6.46447 13.5356c.24395.2439.63993.2439.88388.0L10 10.8839l2.6517 2.6517C12.8956 13.7795 13.2916 13.7795 13.5355 13.5356 13.7795 13.2916 13.7795 12.8956 13.5355 12.6517z" fill="#000"/></svg>
<svg class="faq-icon-plus flex-shrink-0" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M10 0C4.47719.0.0 4.47719.0 10c0 5.5231 4.47719 10 10 10 5.5231.0 10-4.4769 10-10C20 4.47719 15.5231.0 10 0zm0 18.7697c-4.82469.0-8.75-3.945-8.75-8.76974.0-4.82469 3.92531-8.75 8.75-8.75 4.8247.0 8.75 3.92533 8.75 8.75.0 4.82464-3.9253 8.76974-8.75 8.76974zM14.375 9.375h-3.75V5.625C10.625 5.28 10.345 5 10 5s-.625.28-.625.625v3.75H5.625C5.28 9.375 5 9.655 5 10s.28.625.625.625h3.75v3.75C9.375 14.72 9.655 15 10 15S10.625 14.72 10.625 14.375v-3.75h3.75C14.72 10.625 15 10.345 15 10S14.72 9.375 14.375 9.375z" fill="#000"/></svg></div></div><div data-faq-index=8 data-faq-expanded=false class="faq-item flex gap-4 items-start px-6 py-5 rounded-md border duration-200 cursor-pointer bg-gray-50 border-black-100/10"><div class="flex flex-col flex-1 gap-4"><div class="text-base font-bold text-black-100 md:text-lg">I'm not a developer. Can I still use ScrapingBee?</div><div class="faq-answer flex flex-col gap-3 text-sm text-black-100 md:text-base" style=display:none><p>Yes. You don't need to build a scraper from scratch. ScrapingBee integrates with LLM and coding tools via MCP, Skills, and CLI workflows in tools like ChatGPT, Claude, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, and Gemini. It also supports no-code and low-code tools like n8n and Make, plus AI extraction features like AI Query for natural language data extraction.</p></div></div><div class=flex-shrink-0><svg class="faq-icon-close flex-shrink-0" style="display:none" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M17.0711 2.92898c-3.9053-3.90522-10.23695-3.90522-14.14217.0-3.905437 3.90544-3.905216 10.23692.0 14.14212 3.90544 3.9055 10.23667 3.9055 14.14217.0 3.9052-3.9052 3.9054-10.23668.0-14.14212zM3.79889 16.2012C.387325 12.7896.401247 7.22443 3.81284 3.81283c3.41157-3.411566 8.96276-3.411566 12.37436.0 3.4116 3.41157 3.4116 8.96277.0 12.37437C12.7757 19.5988 7.21046 19.6127 3.79889 16.2012zm9.73661-3.5495L10.8