<svg class="faq-icon-plus flex-shrink-0" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M10 0C4.47719.0.0 4.47719.0 10c0 5.5231 4.47719 10 10 10 5.5231.0 10-4.4769 10-10C20 4.47719 15.5231.0 10 0zm0 18.7697c-4.82469.0-8.75-3.945-8.75-8.76974.0-4.82469 3.92531-8.75 8.75-8.75 4.8247.0 8.75 3.92533 8.75 8.75.0 4.82464-3.9253 8.76974-8.75 8.76974zM14.375 9.375h-3.75V5.625C10.625 5.28 10.345 5 10 5s-.625.28-.625.625v3.75H5.625C5.28 9.375 5 9.655 5 10s.28.625.625.625h3.75v3.75C9.375 14.72 9.655 15 10 15S10.625 14.72 10.625 14.375v-3.75h3.75C14.72 10.625 15 10.345 15 10S14.72 9.375 14.375 9.375z" fill="#000"/></svg></div></div><div data-faq-index=9 data-faq-expanded=false class="faq-item flex gap-4 items-start px-6 py-5 rounded-md border duration-200 cursor-pointer bg-gray-50 border-black-100/10"><div class="flex flex-col flex-1 gap-4"><div class="text-base font-bold text-black-100 md:text-lg">Can ScrapingBee render JavaScript and interact with the page before extraction?</div><div class="faq-answer flex flex-col gap-3 text-sm text-black-100 md:text-base" style=display:none><p>Yes. ScrapingBee API can render pages in headless Chrome, wait for elements to load, and perform actions like scrolling, clicking, filling forms, waiting for selectors, and running custom JavaScript for dynamic or multi-step flows.</p></div></div><div class=flex-shrink-0><svg class="faq-icon-close flex-shrink-0" style="display:none" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M17.0711 2.92898c-3.9053-3.90522-10.23695-3.90522-14.14217.0-3.905437 3.90544-3.905216 10.23692.0 14.14212 3.90544 3.9055 10.23667 3.9055 14.14217.0 3.9052-3.9052 3.9054-10.23668.0-14.14212zM3.79889 16.2012C.387325 12.7896.401247 7.22443 3.81284 3.81283c3.41157-3.411566 8.96276-3.411566 12.37436.0 3.4116 3.41157 3.4116 8.96277.0 12.37437C12.7757 19.5988 7.21046 19.6127 3.79889 16.2012zm9.73661-3.5495L10.8839 10l2.6516-2.6516c.244-.24396.244-.63994.0-.88389C13.2916 6.22056 12.8956 6.22056 12.6517 6.46451L10 9.11616 7.34835 6.46451c-.24395-.24395-.63993-.24395-.88388.0-.24396.24395-.24396.639930000000001.0.88389L9.11612 10 6.46447 12.6517C6.22051 12.8956 6.22051 13.2916 6.46447 13.5356c.24395.2439.63993.2439.88388.0L10 10.8839l2.6517 2.6517C12.8956 13.7795 13.2916 13.7795 13.5355 13.5356 13.7795 13.2916 13.7795 12.8956 13.5355 12.6517z" fill="#000"/></svg>
<svg class="faq-icon-plus flex-shrink-0" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M10 0C4.47719.0.0 4.47719.0 10c0 5.5231 4.47719 10 10 10 5.5231.0 10-4.4769 10-10C20 4.47719 15.5231.0 10 0zm0 18.7697c-4.82469.0-8.75-3.945-8.75-8.76974.0-4.82469 3.92531-8.75 8.75-8.75 4.8247.0 8.75 3.92533 8.75 8.75.0 4.82464-3.9253 8.76974-8.75 8.76974zM14.375 9.375h-3.75V5.625C10.625 5.28 10.345 5 10 5s-.625.28-.625.625v3.75H5.625C5.28 9.375 5 9.655 5 10s.28.625.625.625h3.75v3.75C9.375 14.72 9.655 15 10 15S10.625 14.72 10.625 14.375v-3.75h3.75C14.72 10.625 15 10.345 15 10S14.72 9.375 14.375 9.375z" fill="#000"/></svg></div></div><div data-faq-index=10 data-faq-expanded=false class="faq-item flex gap-4 items-start px-6 py-5 rounded-md border duration-200 cursor-pointer bg-gray-50 border-black-100/10"><div class="flex flex-col flex-1 gap-4"><div class="text-base font-bold text-black-100 md:text-lg">What is the difference between the HTML API and dedicated scraper APIs?</div><div class="faq-answer flex flex-col gap-3 text-sm text-black-100 md:text-base" style=display:none><p>The HTML API returns the full page so you can parse it yourself. Dedicated scraper APIs provide structured, ready-to-use data for sources like Amazon, Google Search, YouTube, Walmart, ChatGPT, and Gemini, eliminating the need for custom parsers.</p></div></div><div class=flex-shrink-0><svg class="faq-icon-close flex-shrink-0" style="display:none" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M17.0711 2.92898c-3.9053-3.90522-10.23695-3.90522-14.14217.0-3.905437 3.90544-3.905216 10.23692.0 14.14212 3.90544 3.9055 10.23667 3.9055 14.14217.0 3.9052-3.9052 3.9054-10.23668.0-14.14212zM3.79889 16.2012C.387325 12.7896.401247 7.22443 3.81284 3.81283c3.41157-3.411566 8.96276-3.411566 12.37436.0 3.4116 3.41157 3.4116 8.96277.0 12.37437C12.7757 19.5988 7.21046 19.6127 3.79889 16.2012zm9.73661-3.5495L10.8839 10l2.6516-2.6516c.244-.24396.244-.63994.0-.88389C13.2916 6.22056 12.8956 6.22056 12.6517 6.46451L10 9.11616 7.34835 6.46451c-.24395-.24395-.63993-.24395-.88388.0-.24396.24395-.24396.639930000000001.0.88389L9.11612 10 6.46447 12.6517C6.22051 12.8956 6.22051 13.2916 6.46447 13.5356c.24395.2439.63993.2439.88388.0L10 10.8839l2.6517 2.6517C12.8956 13.7795 13.2916 13.7795 13.5355 13.5356 13.7795 13.2916 13.7795 12.8956 13.5355 12.6517z" fill="#000"/></svg>
<svg class="faq-icon-plus flex-shrink-0" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M10 0C4.47719.0.0 4.47719.0 10c0 5.5231 4.47719 10 10 10 5.5231.0 10-4.4769 10-10C20 4.47719 15.5231.0 10 0zm0 18.7697c-4.82469.0-8.75-3.945-8.75-8.76974.0-4.82469 3.92531-8.75 8.75-8.75 4.8247.0 8.75 3.92533 8.75 8.75.0 4.82464-3.9253 8.76974-8.75 8.76974zM14.375 9.375h-3.75V5.625C10.625 5.28 10.345 5 10 5s-.625.28-.625.625v3.75H5.625C5.28 9.375 5 9.655 5 10s.28.625.625.625h3.75v3.75C9.375 14.72 9.655 15 10 15S10.625 14.72 10.625 14.375v-3.75h3.75C14.72 10.625 15 10.345 15 10S14.72 9.375 14.375 9.375z" fill="#000"/></svg></div></div><div data-faq-index=11 data-faq-expanded=false class="faq-item flex gap-4 items-start px-6 py-5 rounded-md border duration-200 cursor-pointer bg-gray-50 border-black-100/10"><div class="flex flex-col flex-1 gap-4"><div class="text-base font-bold text-black-100 md:text-lg">What is a web scraper API credit?</div><div class="faq-answer flex flex-col gap-3 text-sm text-black-100 md:text-base" style=display:none><p>Each ScrapingBee plan includes a monthly number of web scraper API credits. A basic request costs 1 credit, while features like JavaScript rendering, premium proxies, or AI extraction increase the cost. Pricing is transparent with no hidden fees.</p></div></div><div class=flex-shrink-0><svg class="faq-icon-close flex-shrink-0" style="display:none" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M17.0711 2.92898c-3.9053-3.90522-10.23695-3.90522-14.14217.0-3.905437 3.90544-3.905216 10.23692.0 14.14212 3.90544 3.9055 10.23667 3.9055 14.14217.0 3.9052-3.9052 3.9054-10.23668.0-14.14212zM3.79889 16.2012C.387325 12.7896.401247 7.22443 3.81284 3.81283c3.41157-3.411566 8.96276-3.411566 12.37436.0 3.4116 3.41157 3.4116 8.96277.0 12.37437C12.7757 19.5988 7.21046 19.6127 3.79889 16.2012zm9.73661-3.5495L10.8839 10l2.6516-2.6516c.244-.24396.244-.63994.0-.88389C13.2916 6.22056 12.8956 6.22056 12.6517 6.46451L10 9.11616 7.34835 6.46451c-.24395-.24395-.63993-.24395-.88388.0-.24396.24395-.24396.639930000000001.0.88389L9.11612 10 6.46447 12.6517C6.22051 12.8956 6.22051 13.2916 6.46447 13.5356c.24395.2439.63993.2439.88388.0L10 10.8839l2.6517 2.6517C12.8956 13.7795 13.2916 13.7795 13.5355 13.5356 13.7795 13.2916 13.7795 12.8956 13.5355 12.6517z" fill="#000"/></svg>
