<svg class="faq-icon-plus flex-shrink-0" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M10 0C4.47719.0.0 4.47719.0 10c0 5.5231 4.47719 10 10 10 5.5231.0 10-4.4769 10-10C20 4.47719 15.5231.0 10 0zm0 18.7697c-4.82469.0-8.75-3.945-8.75-8.76974.0-4.82469 3.92531-8.75 8.75-8.75 4.8247.0 8.75 3.92533 8.75 8.75.0 4.82464-3.9253 8.76974-8.75 8.76974zM14.375 9.375h-3.75V5.625C10.625 5.28 10.345 5 10 5s-.625.28-.625.625v3.75H5.625C5.28 9.375 5 9.655 5 10s.28.625.625.625h3.75v3.75C9.375 14.72 9.655 15 10 15S10.625 14.72 10.625 14.375v-3.75h3.75C14.72 10.625 15 10.345 15 10S14.72 9.375 14.375 9.375z" fill="#000"/></svg></div></div><div data-faq-index=17 data-faq-expanded=false class="faq-item flex gap-4 items-start px-6 py-5 rounded-md border duration-200 cursor-pointer bg-gray-50 border-black-100/10"><div class="flex flex-col flex-1 gap-4"><div class="text-base font-bold text-black-100 md:text-lg">What features should the best web scraping API include?</div><div class="faq-answer flex flex-col gap-3 text-sm text-black-100 md:text-base" style=display:none><p>The best web scraping API should handle the hard parts of scraping for you: JavaScript rendering, proxy management, retries, geotargeting, and screenshots.</p><p>It should also support flexible outputs and workflows, including JSON, Markdown, raw or rendered HTML, plain text, AI extraction, search APIs, and dedicated endpoints for specific data sources.</p></div></div><div class=flex-shrink-0><svg class="faq-icon-close flex-shrink-0" style="display:none" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M17.0711 2.92898c-3.9053-3.90522-10.23695-3.90522-14.14217.0-3.905437 3.90544-3.905216 10.23692.0 14.14212 3.90544 3.9055 10.23667 3.9055 14.14217.0 3.9052-3.9052 3.9054-10.23668.0-14.14212zM3.79889 16.2012C.387325 12.7896.401247 7.22443 3.81284 3.81283c3.41157-3.411566 8.96276-3.411566 12.37436.0 3.4116 3.41157 3.4116 8.96277.0 12.37437C12.7757 19.5988 7.21046 19.6127 3.79889 16.2012zm9.73661-3.5495L10.8839 10l2.6516-2.6516c.244-.24396.244-.63994.0-.88389C13.2916 6.22056 12.8956 6.22056 12.6517 6.46451L10 9.11616 7.34835 6.46451c-.24395-.24395-.63993-.24395-.88388.0-.24396.24395-.24396.639930000000001.0.88389L9.11612 10 6.46447 12.6517C6.22051 12.8956 6.22051 13.2916 6.46447 13.5356c.24395.2439.63993.2439.88388.0L10 10.8839l2.6517 2.6517C12.8956 13.7795 13.2916 13.7795 13.5355 13.5356 13.7795 13.2916 13.7795 12.8956 13.5355 12.6517z" fill="#000"/></svg>
<svg class="faq-icon-plus flex-shrink-0" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M10 0C4.47719.0.0 4.47719.0 10c0 5.5231 4.47719 10 10 10 5.5231.0 10-4.4769 10-10C20 4.47719 15.5231.0 10 0zm0 18.7697c-4.82469.0-8.75-3.945-8.75-8.76974.0-4.82469 3.92531-8.75 8.75-8.75 4.8247.0 8.75 3.92533 8.75 8.75.0 4.82464-3.9253 8.76974-8.75 8.76974zM14.375 9.375h-3.75V5.625C10.625 5.28 10.345 5 10 5s-.625.28-.625.625v3.75H5.625C5.28 9.375 5 9.655 5 10s.28.625.625.625h3.75v3.75C9.375 14.72 9.655 15 10 15S10.625 14.72 10.625 14.375v-3.75h3.75C14.72 10.625 15 10.345 15 10S14.72 9.375 14.375 9.375z" fill="#000"/></svg></div></div></div></div></section><script type=application/ld+json>{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A web scraping API is a tool that collects data from websites through an API request. You send a URL and get the page HTML, rendered content, or structured data back. It lets you scrape websites without managing proxies, browsers, retries, or blocking issues yourself."},"name":"What is a web scraping API?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"To use a web scraping API, create an account, get your API key, and send a request to the endpoint you need. Add the target URL and choose options such as JavaScript rendering, proxy type, geotargeting, screenshots, Markdown output, or JSON extraction.\n\nWith ScrapingBee, you can also build the request visually in the dashboard. Choose your endpoint, set your parameters, send a test request, and view the response. To extract data as JSON, use CSS or XPath rules, or describe what you need with AI extraction."},"name":"How do I set up and use a web scraping API?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"With a web scraper API, you can extract data from public web pages, including product listings, prices, reviews, search results, real estate listings, job posts, news articles, company pages, and more. With AI extraction, you can also ask for specific fields in natural language instead of writing custom parsing logic for each website."},"name":"What type of data can I extract with a web scraper API?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. You can automate scraping jobs by calling the API from your backend, scripts, scheduled tasks, no-code workflows, or data pipelines. ScrapingBee handles page fetching, JavaScript rendering, proxies, and anti-bot logic, so your automation can focus on when to run, which URLs to scrape, and where to send the data."},"name":"Can I automate web scraping jobs?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It depends on the target website and the features you enable. Fast Search API requests usually return scraping results in under a second. E-commerce API requests have a median response time of around 2.5 seconds. Standard scraping API requests can take longer when JavaScript rendering, premium proxies, or advanced anti-bot handling are enabled."},"name":"How long does it take to get the scraping results?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"ScrapingBee is built for developers, founders, and product teams that need web data in their apps, workflows, or internal tools. It's ideal for teams that want to collect data at scale without managing proxies, browsers, anti-bot systems, or scraper maintenance. Common use cases include e-commerce, AI, cybersecurity, market intelligence, fintech, and go-to-market tools."},"name":"Who is ScrapingBee built for?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Scraper response times depend on the target website and enabled features. Simple scraping requests are faster, while JavaScript rendering and advanced anti-bot handling take longer. For complex sites, ScrapingBee uses browser rendering with rotating, premium, and stealth proxies so you don't have to build that infrastructure yourself."},"name":"How fast is ScrapingBee's API, and can it handle difficult websites?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. ScrapingBee's web scraper API is SOC 2 Type II compliant, with controls audited and verified by an independent auditor."},"name":"Is ScrapingBee's web scraper API SOC 2 compliant?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. You don't need to build a scraper from scratch. ScrapingBee integrates with LLM and coding tools via MCP, Skills, and CLI workflows in tools like ChatGPT, Claude, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, and Gemini. It also supports no-code and low-code tools like n8n and Make, plus AI extraction features like AI Query for natural language data extraction."},"name":"I'm not a developer. Can I still use ScrapingBee?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. ScrapingBee API can render pages in headless Chrome, wait for elements to load, and perform actions like scrolling, clicking, filling forms, waiting for selectors, and running custom JavaScript for dynamic or multi-step flows."},"name":"Can ScrapingBee render JavaScript and interact with the page before extraction?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The HTML API returns the full page so you can parse it yourself. Dedicated scraper APIs provide structured, ready-to-use data for sources like Amazon, Google Search, YouTube, Walmart, ChatGPT, and Gemini, eliminating the need for custom parsers."},"name":"What is the difference between the HTML API and dedicated scraper APIs?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Each ScrapingBee plan includes a monthly number of web scraper API credits. A basic request costs 1 credit, while features like JavaScript rendering, premium proxies, or AI extraction increase the cost. Pricing is transparent with no hidden fees."},"name":"What is a web scraper API credit?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You can upgrade your plan for the current month, renew early, or purchase one-time add-ons without waiting for the next billing cycle."},"name":"What happens if I run out of credits before my subscription renews?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. You get 1,000 free web scraping API credits when you sign up, with no credit card required."},"name":"Can I try ScrapingBee before choosing a paid plan?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"ScrapingBee only charges for successful scraping requests, defined as those returning HTTP 200, 404 or 410 status codes."},"name":"What happens if a scraping request fails?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. You can cancel anytime from your dashboard in under 30 seconds."},"name":"Can I cancel my plan at any time?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The Business+ plan includes 400 concurrent scraper API requests. If you need more, our Custom plans offer additional concurrency. Feel free to reach out to our sales team to discuss your specific requirements."},"name":"Can I get more concurrency?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The best web scraping API should handle the hard parts of scraping for you: JavaScript rendering, proxy management, retries, geotargeting, and screenshots.\n\nIt should also support flexible outputs and workflows, including JSON, Markdown, raw or rendered HTML, plain text, AI extraction, search APIs, and dedicated endpoints for specific data sources."},"name":"What features should the best web scraping API include?"}]}</script><script>(function(){var e=null,t=document.querySelectorAll("#faqs .faq-item");t.forEach(function(t){t.dataset.faqExpanded==="true"&&(e=parseInt(t.dataset.faqIndex))}),t.forEach(function(n){n.addEventListener("click",function(){var s,o,i,a=parseInt(n.dataset.faqIndex);t.forEach(function(e){var t=e.querySelector(".faq-answer"),n=e.querySelector(".faq-icon-close"),s=e.querySelector(".faq-icon-plus");e.classList.remove("bg-yellow-100","border-[#BD9002]"),e.classList.add("bg-gray-50","border-black-100/10"),t&&(t.style.display="none"),n&&(n.style.display="none"),s&&(s.style.display="")}),e===a?e=null:(e=a,s=n.querySelector(".faq-answer"),o=n.querySelector(".faq-icon-close"),i=n.querySelector(".faq-icon-plus"),n.classList.remove("bg-gray-50","border-black-100/10"),n.classList.add("bg-yellow-100","border-[#BD9002]"),s&&(s.style.display=""),o&&(o.style.display=""),i&&(i.style.display="none"))})})})()</script></div></main><footer class="bg-black-100 relative text-white pt-[80px] md:pt-[180px] lg:pt-[80px] pb-[50px] z-[100] text-center sm:text-left overflow-hidden"><div class="container max-w-full"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center pb-[40px] md:pb-[70px] lg:pb-[113px] mb-[30px] md:mb-[48px] border-b border-white border-opacity-20"><div class="w-full sm:flex-1 mb-[30px] sm:mb-[0] pr-[10px] sm:pr-[20px]"><h2 class="text-[28px] sm:text-[36px] md:text-[48px] lg:text-[56px] leading-[1.21] tracking-[0.2px] mb-[5px]">Ready to get started?</h2><p class="text-[14px] md:text-[16px]">Get access to 1,000 free scraper API credits, no credit card required!</p></div><div class="w-full sm:w-auto sm:flex-shrink-0 sm:text-right lg:mr-[86px]"><a href=https://dashboard.scrapingbee.com/account/register class="btn btn-yellow px-[30px] sm:px-[37px] w-full sm:w-auto">Try ScrapingBee for Free</a></div></div><div class="flex flex-wrap -mx-[10px] sm:-mx-[15px] md:-mx-[20px]"><div class="w-full md:w-1/4 px-[10px] sm:px-[15px] md:px-[20px] mb-[30px] md:mb-[0]"><div class="logo mb-[25px]"><a href=/><img src=/images/logo-white.svg width=164 height=28 class=inline-block alt=ScrapingBee loading=lazy></a></div><p class=mb-[18px]>ScrapingBee API handles headless browsers and rotates proxies for you.</p><ul class="flex flex-wrap justify-center sm:justify-start -mx-[11px]"><li class=px-[11px]><a href=https://x.c